    "lcm_example": {
      "id": "lcm_example",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The chapter's example asks for the least number that is:\n\n1. divisible by 16, 20 and 24\n2. also a perfect square.\n\nStep 1: find the L.C.M.\n\nL.C.M.(16, 20, 24) = 240\n\nSo 240 is the least number that satisfies the divisibility requirement.\n\nBut 240 is not yet the required answer because the question also requires a perfect square.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "factor_240"
        }
      ]
    },
    "factor_240": {
      "id": "factor_240",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now inspect 240 in prime-factor form.\n\n240 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 3 × 5\n\nSo we can group it as:\n\n240 = 2^4 × 3 × 5\n\nThe source then looks at the prime-factor powers.\n\nThe power of 2 is already paired:\n\n2^4\n\nBut 3 and 5 each occur only once.\n\nThe source therefore multiplies by:\n\n3 × 5\n\nto make those factors paired as well.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "factor_check"
        }
      ]
    },
