      "content": {
        "text": "Let's run the whole method one last time without skipping any step.\n\nQuestion:\n\nFind the least perfect square divisible by 16, 20 and 24.\n\nStep 1:\nFind the L.C.M.\n\nL.C.M.(16,20,24) = 240\n\nStep 2:\nPrime-factorize the L.C.M.\n\n240 = 2^4 × 3 × 5\n\nStep 3:\nInspect the factors.\n\n2 has four copies.\n3 has one copy.\n5 has one copy.\n\nStep 4:\nMultiply by the missing copies used by the source:\n\n3 × 5\n\nStep 5:\nCalculate:\n\n240 × 3 × 5 = 3600\n\nStep 6:\nRecognize the result as:\n\n3600 = 60^2\n\nAnswer:\n\n3600",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
