      "content": {
        "text": "Excellent.\n\nThis subtopic has one main pattern:\n\nFirst satisfy the divisibility condition with L.C.M.\n\nThen satisfy the perfect-square condition by looking at the prime-factor form of that L.C.M. and multiplying by the missing prime factors used in the chapter's solution.\n\nThe source example:\n\nL.C.M.(16,20,24) = 240\n240 = 2^4 × 3 × 5\nextra multiplier = 3 × 5\nrequired number = 240 × 3 × 5 = 3600\n\nAnd:\n\n3600 = 60^2\n\nThe matching objective question has the same answer:\n\n3600.\n\nSo when you see:\n\n'least number'\n+ 'divisible by these numbers'\n+ 'perfect square'\n\nthink:\n\nL.C.M. first\n→ inspect prime factors\n→ add the missing copies\n→ final square.",
